ived | **Refuted** |\n| Reflected caster’s central targeting sufficiency | **Evidence-unknown** |\n\nI left the second candidate unused: the evidence did not establish a materially different repair beyond another healing-phase guess.\n\nThe bundle’s folder labels were inconsistent. I used the actual R91 C2 found under `duty_conflict_parent_c2`, and verified the actual R92 contrast artifacts against their closeout hashes. Candidate lineage, hashes, dependencies, regression observations, risks, and `MODEL_GAP` are recorded in the frozen [plan and validation card](/home/bigdata/Desktop/arknights-auto-planner/docs/review/fc77177/real_tool_closed_loop_sol_high_seven_retry2_v1/session/candidates/candidate-001/simulation/plan_snapshot.json). The [final status](/home/bigdata/Desktop/arknights-auto-planner/docs/review/fc77177/real_tool_closed_loop_sol_high_seven_retry2_v1/session/candidates/candidate-001/simulation/final_status.json) records the complete LOSS.\n\nFinal ledger: **CLI 1/1; checks 2/10; candidates 1/2; simulations 1/2**, with one complete simulation. Configured model **gpt-6.1-sol/high**, K=7, mechanics **`m38b-2781-animation-speed-v1`**, controlled runner. No input/output/cached-token usage record was visible before this final response; those counts remain **UNKNOWN**, as does **`UNKNOWN_CLI_INTERNAL`**. `cached_input` is an input subset and is not additive. Findings apply only to this fixed simulator.",
